Modified the transaction handling in server/api.php to support partial success when processing a batch of SKUs.
Instead of rolling back the entire transaction if some SKUs fail to be created, the transaction is now always committed, saving the successfully processed items.
In case of partial failure, the API now returns a 207 Multi-Status code.
The response body for partial failures has been updated to include both the processedSkus (with statuses 'exists' or 'created') and a detailed errors array, allowing the client to understand what succeeded and what failed.